## 3. Standard Change Request (RFC) Template

```yaml
change_id: CR-2026-104
title: Enforce SSH Key-Only Authentication on Production Linux Bastion
owner: <security-engineer>
stakeholders: [SOC Team, Linux Infrastructure, DevOps]
risk_level: Medium
impact_analysis: Disables password-based SSH logins; users without registered public keys will lose access.
test_results: Validated on staging-bastion-01; key-based login succeeded, password auth rejected.
maintenance_window: Sunday 02:00 - 03:00 UTC
sop_steps:
  1. Verify all authorized public keys exist in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys.
  2. Backup /etc/ssh/sshd_config to /etc/ssh/sshd_config.bak.
  3. Set PasswordAuthentication no and reload sshd (systemctl reload sshd).
  4. Validate new SSH session before closing active admin session.
backout_plan: Restore /etc/ssh/sshd_config.bak and run systemctl reload sshd via out-of-band console.